1
00:00:00,915 --> 00:00:02,295
(Sheldon:)A, I rarely kid.

2
00:00:02,458 --> 00:00:06,878
(Sheldon:)And B, when I do kid, you will know it
by my use of the word "buzzinga."

3
00:00:07,505 --> 00:00:11,385
(Howard:)So you're saying the two of you are
going to be sleeping in the same bed?

4
00:00:11,592 --> 00:00:12,972
(Howard:)Yes.

5
00:00:13,469 --> 00:00:15,299
Buzzinga.

6
00:00:18,599 --> 00:00:20,179
(Sheldon:)Leonard?

7
00:00:20,351 --> 00:00:21,891
(Leonard:)Thank you.

8
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:26,270
Why is a renowned scientist staying
in our apartment instead of a hotel?

9
00:00:26,482 --> 00:00:28,942
(Sheldon:)She doesn't care for hotels.
And who can blame her?

10
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:31,780
(Sheldon:)Windows that don't open,
multi-user linens...

11
00:00:31,988 --> 00:00:33,618
(Sheldon:)...keys shaped like credit cards.

12
00:00:33,781 --> 00:00:36,701
(Sheldon:)As if one walks around
with unassigned slots in one's wallet.

13
00:00:37,285 --> 00:00:39,995
(Sheldon:)All right, I believe I have time
for one more question.

14
00:00:40,163 --> 00:00:41,203
[RAJESH CLEARS THROAT]

15
00:00:41,372 --> 00:00:42,702
(Sheldon:)Yes, Raj?

16
00:00:42,874 --> 00:00:44,874
RAJESH:
When can I sit with you again?

17
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:48,592
When I've seen two negative
throat cultures spaced 12 hours apart.

18
00:00:48,754 --> 00:00:50,044
(Sheldon:)You know the drill.

19
00:00:50,214 --> 00:00:51,844
(Sheldon:)All right, if you'll excuse me...

20
00:00:52,008 --> 00:00:55,638
(Sheldon:)...I am off to start
a prophylactic course of antibiotics.

21
00:00:57,555 --> 00:01:00,645
(Leonard:)I can't believe he's friends
with Elizabeth Plimpton.

22
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:03,390
(Leonard:)I can't believe
they let him into Canada.

23
00:01:03,603 --> 00:01:06,313
(Howard:)Whoa. You heard the man.
Where's your throat cultures?

24
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:09,320
(Howard:)-Kidding. Sit down.
LEONARD: Ha.

25
00:01:10,776 --> 00:01:18,036
[SNEEZES]

